WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.420
AI-generated documentation must be reviewed by humans.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:14.520
Models can miss context, merge unrelated items, misunderstand architecture, overstate confidence, or infer details not present in the source material.

3
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.460
Human review should include source verification, owner confirmation, and checks for unsupported claims.

4
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.840
The review process is what turns a generated draft into a defensible artifact.

5
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.240
Version control is a practical maintenance tool.

6
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:37.980
Documentation can live beside code, infrastructure, or architecture records, and updates can be reviewed through pull requests or another controlled workflow.

7
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.600
The important idea is that changes are visible, attributable, and connected to system changes.

8
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.740
Silent edits make trust harder to maintain.

9
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.860
Define change triggers.

10
00:00:48.960 --> 00:01:02.960
New APIs, changed authentication flows, new cloud resources, new data stores, new vendors, changed network exposure, deployment architecture changes, and incident findings should all trigger documentation review.

11
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:09.940
Scheduled refreshes are useful, but they should not be the only mechanism because systems can drift quickly between review cycles.

12
00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:20.060
Drift detection can be supported by comparing documentation against source material such as infrastructure exports, API specs, repository metadata, or deployment manifests.

13
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:27.280
AI can help identify mismatches and create review prompts, but owners should still confirm the result.

14
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:31.860
The goal is to catch stale documentation before it misleads risk decisions.

15
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.500
Measure documentation usefulness, not just existence.

16
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:45.600
Useful documentation answers reviewer questions, reduces repeated discovery work, supports threat modeling, helps incident responders, and makes uncertainty visible.

17
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.940
If the document is polished but no one trusts it or updates it, the workflow has failed.

18
00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.600
Maintenance is part of the product.
